        "id": 3616462
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-22T01:34:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. There is an mm lock contention issue with process_madvise(). When the app switches to the background while process_madvise is executing, and then switches back to the foreground, there will be a 1-second stutter.\n2. Android reclaims background processes only when the app switches to the cache state. We need to implement freezing and partial compression when the app is not in the foreground, and full compression when the app has been in the background for a long time.\n3. Compression based on memcg is simpler to implement than compression based on processes.",
      "parentUuid": "9c97247a_76889207",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4405,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4405,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "188a460740bbaad4b6a47de84fa456e8acf767e2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
