      "writtenOn": "2025-01-22T19:22:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. So, I\u0027m guessing you are implementing something like partial MADV_PAGEOUT. And you would still need to hold the mmap_lock, just for a shorter amount of time?\n\nWouldn\u0027t it be easier to export `do_madvise()` instead and add a hook inside `madvise_cold_or_pageout_pte_range()` to terminate the loop earlier to limit the number of isolated pages and then reclaim them? That seems like a more straight-forward and ribust approach than exporting individual internal functions.",
      "parentUuid": "94e40a6f_caf1ac70",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4405,
        "startChar": 0,
